; ENUM (RFC 6116) for the test numbers. They are in the 555-0100 to
; 555-0199 range that the North American Numbering Plan keeps for
; fiction, so no real line is named. Each NAPTR turns the number into
; the SIP URI of that number in the home domain, which is a public
; identity of the subscriber that holds it.
$ORIGIN e164.arpa.
$TTL 60
@  IN SOA dns.ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org. hostmaster.ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org. 3 3600 600 86400 60
@  IN NS  dns.ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org.

; +1 202 555 0101, reversed digit by digit (RFC 6116 3.2).
1.0.1.0.5.5.5.2.0.2.1 IN NAPTR 10 100 "u" "E2U+sip" "!^.*$!sip:+12025550101@ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org!" .
; +1 202 555 0102
